 # bench-locale-pack (benchmark fixture)
 
-A 19-language override layer for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), written in the
-0.1.1-era style: it patches the locale runtime's lookup chain so a selected
-third language wins over DSH's native zh/en while DSH's active locale stays
-on `en`, ships a custom switcher row into the settings General section, and
-persists the selection in localStorage (`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`).
-Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub. The host is moving to
-dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A 19-language pack for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), delivered as a client-only
+plugin through the native locale service that shipped in dsh 0.1.2-alpha.1:
+the browser half adds each curated language to the shared catalog
+(`ctx.locale.addLanguage({ id, label, fallback: 'en' })`) and registers every
+namespace × language dictionary (`ctx.locale.register(ns, lang, dict)`), with
+per-key fallback to DSH's native zh/en. The switcher is the harness's own
+Language row in Settings → General (slot `settings.general.item`), which lists
+every registered language, and the selection persists as `locale.preference`
+in the host settings. The host half is a no-op stub — no runtime work. The
+host is on dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+
+`client.js` is the package's `./client` artifact. client-modules serves that
+file verbatim inside the page's shared bundle script, so it registers itself
+through `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id: '<package.json name>', factory })`
+(entry, module, and registration ids all equal the package name); a bare ESM
+module there is a parse error for the whole composed bundle.
+
+## Retired 0.1.1-era surface
+
+Each entry point of the pre-migration design is now covered by
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale` at the same slot, setting, or service, so the
+plugin no longer carries its own copy:
+
+| 0.1.1-era entry point | Official entry point that covers it |
+|---|---|
+| LocaleRuntime lookup-chain monkey-patch (third language wins while DSH stays on `en`) | `addLanguage` + `register` fallback chain (`ja → en`, per key) |
+| custom switcher row in Settings → General (`settings.general.item`) | the locale package's Language row in the same slot |
+| localStorage store `dsh-plugin-better-locale:active` | host-backed `locale.preference` setting |
+| plugin-provided `betterLocale` service for third-party dictionaries | public `ctx.locale` registration API |
+
+The browser half imports the legacy localStorage value once and hands it to
+`ctx.locale.setLocale`, so an existing selection survives the upgrade.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
